WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Start with the capsule and the subcapsular sinus beneath it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Lymph from tissue enters afferent lymphatics and the sinus system.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
It passes toward medullary sinuses and leaves via an efferent lymphatic at the hilum.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Pause and predict: is the high endothelial venule a lymphatic vessel?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
No. An HEV is a blood vessel. Circulating lymphocytes can cross it into the paracortex.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Keep lymph flow and lymphocyte entry from blood as separate routes.
